1071 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-2,4)}\\sqrt[3]{xy}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344993 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3f277d23-3dcb-54b8-9f1f-cefa2a015d92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344993 #edb/ref 1074 "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{xy}.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous for all values of $x$ and $y.$ So,  we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(-2,4)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2,4)}\\sqrt[3]{xy}=\\sqrt{(-2)\\cdot 4}=\\sqrt[3]{-8}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345005 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345005 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74966" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345005 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345005 #edb/ref 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345005 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "56c07c72-df51-5ec4-88ac-9185b7690371" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345005 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\cdot 0\\cdot {0}^{3}}{{0}^{6}+8\\cdot {0}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nLet's attempt to evaluate the limit approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{{x}^{6}+8{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}({x}^{4}+8)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+8} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{3}}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{{x}^{6}+8{x}^{6}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{9{x}^{6}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186377699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "117ca5de-bfde-5504-8e9b-162dc1ee9296" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3d118fc5-1c52-5566-be98-a9707e774937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377698 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377698 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377698 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "30aa323e-111a-55db-ae16-f96b2c70da3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377699 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377699 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377699 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "563f0bf5-f3be-54dc-b44e-fce9a03892d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377700 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377700 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377700 #edb/ref 1