 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "da8b2db2-4123-5665-b738-98ed34b75b3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378625 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378625 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378625 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d3687c4-99c4-5acf-aa17-8ee4a667504b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378626 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378626 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378626 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5cfdc49f-f710-579f-a121-34bd82cc68c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378627 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378627 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378627 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5bef6f1c-9c50-5077-83d6-7937a6ae0e70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378628 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378628 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378628 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6b4dca40-4471-5b61-bf8b-e5086c017493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378636 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186378637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378636 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129403" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378636 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378636 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine ${lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378636 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a45c5a39-df0e-5ca7-830f-279fde3ab785" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378636 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}-{0}^{2}}{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0}{0+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nLet's attempt to evaluate the limit approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{0}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{0}{2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378637 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f471c6a4-8548-5953-bc64-722a32227684" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378638 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378638 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378638 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ed9a8298-54cd-5904-87cc-0773ceed9484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378639 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378639 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378639 #edb/ref 1083 