] [17592186407845 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407845 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407845 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407845 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407845 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407845 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407845 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186407828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407845 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e093674e-caf5-5f8d-97ff-ca3172fa6889" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407847 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186454690 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186407847 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186454691 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186407847 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186454692 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186407847 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36139" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407847 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407847 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$\n- **II.** The limit evaluates to $-1$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2}$\n- **III.** The limit exists and is equal to $\\frac{1}{3}$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186407847 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9a907de-0404-5ffb-8362-e9676298070b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407847 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+2\\cdot 0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=-{x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2(-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407849 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407849 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407849 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407849 #edb/ref 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{y+z}{\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407849 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fac05de1-cec1-5741-a5ec-beb8567ada24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407849 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{y+z}{\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z}} & =\\frac{1+(-1)}{\\sqrt{2-1}-\\sqrt{2+(-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{y+z}{\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{(y+z)(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})}{(\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z})(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{(y+z)(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})}{(x-y)-(x+z)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{(y+z)(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})}{-(y+z)} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{\\cancel{(y+z)}(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})}{\\cancel{(y+z)}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z}) & =-(\\sqrt{2-1}+\\sqrt{2+(-1)}) \\\\  & =-(1+1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "23171e8d-210d-5c2c-9bfd-bb23fda5150e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186377708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "61b825c0-1272-5e4c-b3ff-4f0f75ec0886" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "80843e02-eff6-534a-9c80-13ab1c07a9fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407853 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407853 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dd8e3137-e924-50eb-b2e3-83c1445d70ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407853 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407854 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e8e33d31-3246-51ca-a270-794ee881c78b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407854 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186428460 #edb/ref 1030 0.6666666666666666 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428460 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captur